00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.663
- So what I do, I do in neuroscience.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.650
So basically, my lab,

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:15.550
main focus is to build these
big, incredible microscope

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:18.530
in order to look directly
in to the mouse brain

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.540
or other animals brain.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.940
I do mouse things and stuff,
so that's why I say mouse,

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:29.850
but you can see into a
monkey's brain, a fish brain,

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.190
sea elegans brain, like worm's brain.

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:34.830
And the idea is I like to
see the neural activity

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:38.190
and figure out what's
going on in the brain

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:42.040
and understand the algorithms
that the brain is using

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.070
in order to encode information

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:49.070
and also decoding information
from its own coding

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.000
and then to perceive and
be able to move, et cetera.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.320
So it's very interesting.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:00.320
And today, basically, I'm
gonna give you a broad tour

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.820
of how my things look like.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:07.270
I'm gonna explain to you
a smaller experiments

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:08.823
that I'm running right now.

00:01:10.233 --> 00:01:11.990
And hopefully, we get to the
point that I can show you

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:15.740
how to put the animals
and we do experiments.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:20.740
So, I'm gonna share the
other screen that I have.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:27.350
So what I do is just, I look
at the mouse's brain directly,

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.320
but the important thing is
to look at the mouse's brain

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.070
while the animal is executing a behavior.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:38.500
So I have a pretty, specific behavior

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:43.500
because I'm studying how
the brain encodes for time,

00:01:44.897 --> 00:01:48.340
for how the time is passing.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:53.340
So normally, we are pretty aware
of how much time has passed

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:56.710
between two very
important salient stimuli.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:59.240
And the idea is to try to understand

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:02.440
how is the brain keeping
track of this timing?

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:05.860
So, I train the animals

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:09.540
to perceive two different time intervals.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:13.610
One is gonna be short,
so it's of half a second,

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:17.280
and the other one is a long
time interval of two seconds.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.040
For the animal, this is long, you know?

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.540
For us, it's very fast,
but if you do it too long,

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:24.383
then the mouse can get distracted.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:30.210
So what I do in order to study that,

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:33.903
now I'm gonna share the screen of this,

00:02:35.276 --> 00:02:37.893
the screen here.

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:43.790
Okay, yeah, you can see the screen.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.290
This is the first time
that I do it like this.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.640
So let me know if you have any problems.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:51.110
So what I'm going to use

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:53.633
in order for the animal to basically,

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:58.660
perceive these two intervals of time

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:00.370
and also make sure the animal

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:03.140
is actually paying attention to this,

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:06.223
is I'm gonna implement a
system that's called two,

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.800
this is not working

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:12.950
two, forced choice task.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:14.520
So the animal has two,

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.750
basically, what is gonna happen

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.150
is that I'm gonna give the animal

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:21.990
these two different stimuli,

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:23.010
which is the interval.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:28.010
And it's given by applying one
tone on a specific frequency

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:30.130
at the beginning of one trial.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:33.490
And then the time interval is gonna pass

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:37.025
between when I applied the second tone,

00:03:37.025 --> 00:03:38.250
this is the second stimuli.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.303
So in the case of a short interval,

00:03:40.303 --> 00:03:43.270
it's gonna be half a second as I said.

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:45.030
And if it's a long interval,

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:47.983
the second tone is gonna come later,

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:53.360
at the two seconds around, okay?

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:56.520
So the animal has to basically
perceive these two tones.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.423
And then the animal has to tell me,

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:04.380
basically if it perceive
a long or short interval.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:09.380
So I'm gonna just present
the animal to a water spout

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:13.400
so the animal can then...

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:18.400
So if I have the mouse,
like I have a mouse, here,

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:25.550
the mouse is gonna
perceive these two tones.

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:29.560
And then it's gonna have two spouts

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:32.810
where water is gonna come out of.

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:34.270
And the animal has to,

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:37.900
if it perceived, by example, a short tone,

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.520
the animal has to lick from one spout

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:42.170
and then it's gonna get the water reward.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:43.820
If it licks from the other spout,

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:45.470
then it's gonna get a punishment.

00:04:48.417 --> 00:04:50.630
And if the animal perceives a long tone,

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:55.367
then the animal needs to start
licking to the other spout.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:02.960
So that's why it's called
a two forced choice task

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:06.170
because the animal has
only two choices to make.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:09.160
So you're forcing the
animal to make two choices

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.970
and it's either licking right or left.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:13.282
And in this case, for example,

00:05:13.282 --> 00:05:14.900
if it licks to the right,

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:15.840
it's gonna represent

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:19.503
that the animal perceive a short interval.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:26.310
And if it licks to the
left, it's a long interval.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:31.310
So I'm gonna be training these
animals to be doing this.

